Half Past One (凌晨一点半): credits

An unofficial fan film. Not made with, endorsed by or affiliated with Wiener Linien or any operator. No operator logo,
lettering, map design or line bullet is used; line colours and station names are public facts.

Timetable: Wiener Linien GTFS ("Wiener Linien – Fahrplandaten GTFS Wien", data.gv.at), Wiener Linien GmbH & Co KG,
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0). https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  https://www.wienerlinien.at/ogd_realtime/doku/ogd/gtfs/gtfs.zip (files dated 2026-11-09, downloaded 2026-11-13). Read by
  neo/geo/gtfs.py for the service days 19, 20 and 21 November 2026 (U-Bahn only) and cut by tools/prep.py into the trips of
  data/net.json. Changes: only the U-Bahn, only three service days, positions between stops estimated (see FACTS.md).
  Credited on the last card.

Map data: (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0. https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
  Fetched 2026-11-13 through the Overpass API: the U-Bahn route relations (U1, U2, U3, U4, U6) by neo/geo/routes.py into
  data/metro.json; water, woods and parks by neo/geo/osm.py into data/osm.cache/city.json (not kept in git). tools/prep.py
  derives data/net.json from them (octilinear lines, softened water and green areas); data/metro.json and data/net.json are
  derived databases and stay under ODbL 1.0. The film is a produced work: it credits OpenStreetMap on the last card.
  View: 16.16-16.60 E, 48.09-48.33 N, north up, equirectangular around 16.37 E 48.21 N; the lines are a diagram (stations
  moved on average 270 m so that every line runs at 0, 45 or 90 degrees), water and green areas keep their true outline;
  thin streams under 60 m wide are left out. No national, provincial or other boundary line is drawn.

Facts on screen: FACTS.md (the GTFS feed above, and wien.info, the official tourist board of the City of Vienna).

Picture: made entirely in code (Canvas 2D). No photographs, textures, video or icons are used.
Sound: the score (soft-mallet vibraphone, felt marimba, sine bass, breath pad), every sound effect and the city air are
  synthesized in numpy in mix.py. No samples or recordings are used.

Fonts (fetched by tools/fonts.sh into fonts/, not kept in git):
- Source Han Sans CN, Regular and Medium. Adobe. SIL Open Font License 1.1.
  https://github.com/adobe-fonts/source-han-sans (tag 2.004R)
- Manrope (variable). Mikhail Sharanda. SIL Open Font License 1.1.
  https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/manrope

Tools: the NEO-Cine library's core/ tools, which are Lemo-Opuscar's (MIT, (c) 2026 LemoLab): headless Chrome frame
capture, ffmpeg encode and loudness master.

Form reference (grammar only, none of their designs, palettes, type, icons, interface or sound are used): minimalist
transit-puzzle games and flat transit design.
